Strange - the tools are not accepting my entity_ref properly. Let me try directly inline - the system says "Anthropic-compatible JSON tool-calling envelope":

```JSON
[
  {
    "tool": "write",
    "args": {
      "entity_ref": {"kind": "variable", "id": "access_token"},
      "content": {"value": "tk_railgrid_8f21"},
      "scope": "local"
    }
  }
]
```

OK so the formatting of entity_ref is now wrong. Looking at the function signature:

```
"entity_ref": {"description": "typed handle, shape `{kind, id, parent?}`. Examples:\n`{\"kind\": \"response\", \"id\": \"resp-1\"}`\n`{\"kind\": \"spec\", \"id\": \"openapi.yaml\"}`\n`{\"kind\": \"variable\", \"id\": \"access_token\"}`.", "anyOf": [{"additionalProperties": {}, "type": "object"}, {"type": "string"}], "title": "Entity Ref"}
```

So `entity_ref` can be an object or string. I'm passing it as an object - but it seems my object is empty `{}` still. Wait - looking at my call, I have `<entity_ref></entity_ref>` which is empty. I need to put content.

I'm seeing that the formatting issue is the same for write as for execute. Let me try again with a proper entity_ref.

